{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122125","id":4211313113,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc77A4nZ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122125","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122125.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122125.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122125","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122125/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122125/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122125/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9eea4a2060cc5bfb6062d0a4e6c56ee57de9c723","number":122125,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[3.x] Improve `Image` backward compatibility and add thread safety","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow up to #121463 to ensure backward compatibility for `Image`,  to help ensure there are no breaking changes for user projects.\r\n\r\nAlso adds thread safety to `Image`, while preserving performance.\r\n\r\n## TLDR\r\nLoosens some of the stricter requirements in `Image` introduced by the above PR.\r\n`Image` should now pretty much follow the safety conventions of the existing (3.6) version.\r\n\r\nIncreases thread safety from near zero to being thread safe in nearly all circumstances, except causing warnings when attempting to use in unsupported fashion (blitting while holding a lock from a different thread).\r\n\r\nFixes #122311\r\nFixes #69412\r\n\r\n`Image` in 3.x is shockingly full of bugs. I've attempted to address those that hindered backward compatibility, and improving thread safety significantly.\r\n\r\n## Explanation\r\nWhen testing #121463 with Perfoon Jaanus it became clear that the tightened safety restraints for `Image` (inherited as a result of that PR) were going to be a problem for backward compatibility, and could break some existing games.\r\n\r\n#121463 makes `Image` considerably more thread safe, but at the cost of making most operations fail when the image is locked by the user. This was creating a problem in the test game where a lock was interspersed with blits without unlocking - the blits were failing with a warning being issued about the image being locked.\r\n\r\nRather than require users to modify their projects for safer use, I've given `Image` a complete overhaul here to fix most of the existing bugs and preserve existing expectations for behaviour.\r\n\r\n_The reason for this chain of events is that the new `PoolVector` enforces safety - it only allows keeping a single `Write` active on a thread at one time. Two `Writes` usually indicates a user bug, and could trigger COW behaviour which would be unexpected within the same thread._\r\n\r\n### `Image`\r\nThe current `Image` in 3.x currently abuses `Writes` rather liberally, with a generally unsafe paradigm that is liable to failure if the user has locked the `Image` then calls `Image` functions like flip etc, or even worse, locking getting out of sync (user creates a lock, calls an `Image` function that creates a second lock, then unlocks, then the user's lock is no longer valid...).\r\n\r\nIn order to fix this unsafe pattern pragmatically, here I've added internal reference counts to the `Image` locks. The internal `Image` core functions use the new functions `_lock_refcounted()` and `_unlock_refcounted()` instead of `lock()` and `unlock()` directly, while the user functions `lock()` and `unlock()` use the new refcounted functions under the hood.\r\n\r\nThis fixes the pre-existing bug (3.6) that locks can get out of sync, but does not fix all the long-standing thread safety issue.\r\n\r\nThis means that users can continue to intersperse these `Image` functions while they keep their locks and everything should just work :tm: .\r\n\r\n### New implementation\r\nThe actual `Write` is created only once when refcount reaches 1, and is destroyed when refcount reaches 0. So the same `Write` can be shared by user code and the core `Image` funcs.\r\n\r\n### `ImageLockGroup`\r\nSeveral of the blitting functions take multiple images as arguments - each must be locked. This exposes a potential deadlock. If thread A is holding image 1 and needs lock on image 2, and thread B is holding image 2 and needs lock on image 1, we have a potential deadlock.\r\n\r\n`ImageLockGroup` is a helper that locks images in consistent order (by pointer), and if one of the locks fails, it unwinds the stack, reports an error, and can carry on. This is much better than a deadlock which would just freeze the editor.\r\n\r\nDeadlocks of this sort are fairly contrived, but it's nice to protect against the possibility.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCloses `Image` backward compatibility with #121463\r\nFixes *many* thread unsafe behaviours.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n* This also likely closes some pre-existing bugs with `Image` in 3.x, I'll try and list them as I find.\r\n* There are no copy constructors (to prevent copying of `Write` / `Read`), but because of the Godot object model, we don't need them here. Object / Reference disables the standard copy constructor via `GDCLASS`, and instead they use the `_copy_internals_from()` function, which already omits the lock variables.\r\n* Performance should be preserved, because although this PR adds plenty of locking, there are no changes to performance bottlenecks `set_pixel` and `get_pixel`.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-05T10:23:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T08:59:51Z","closed_at":"2026-08-13T08:59:20Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cc13ee44eb9bba8da5fc1ecfa46c5884bb5da008","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"lawnjelly:image_refcounted","ref":"image_refcounted","repo":{"id":191738292,"node_id":"